1. R5: Rapid Realistic Routing on Real-world and Reimagined networks
==============================================================================

https://github.com/conveyal/r5 (version 7.6, the one r5r 2.5.0 runs)

The routing logic of peabiru is a port of R5 to Rust: the construction of
the street network from OpenStreetMap (osm/, street/), the loading of GTFS
and the transit layer (gtfs/, transit/), the checks the GTFS library in
R5's source tree (com.conveyal.gtfs) makes while loading a feed
(gtfs/validate.rs, gtfs/population.rs), the street router, the RAPTOR
search over a departure window with Monte Carlo draws for frequency-based
trips, the propagation of travel times to destinations, the decay functions
and the travel-time, accessibility, expanded and arrival-time results. The
code was written in Rust for this project from R5's source, following its
algorithms, constants and tie-breaking rules step by step so that the results
are the same; it is therefore a work derived from R5. R5 is distributed under
