2. Apache Commons Math 3.0
==============================================================================

https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-math/ (version 3.0, the one
bundled in the R5 7.6 jar)

Three files are translations to Rust of parts of Apache Commons Math:

  fastmath.rs  org.apache.commons.math3.util.FastMath: the method
               exp(double, double, double[]) and the contents of the tables
               FastMath.ExpIntTable (EXP_INT_TABLE_A, EXP_INT_TABLE_B) and
               FastMath.ExpFracTable (EXP_FRAC_TABLE_A, EXP_FRAC_TABLE_B).
  fastmath_trig.rs
               org.apache.commons.math3.util.FastMath: the methods
               toRadians, doubleHighPart, sin, cos, sinQ, cosQ, polySine,
               polyCosine, asin, atan(double, double, boolean), pow(double,
               double) and log(double, double[]) (without the Payne-Hanek
               reduction), and the contents of the tables SINE_TABLE_A/B,
               COSINE_TABLE_A/B, TANGENT_TABLE_A/B, EIGHTHS,
               LN_HI_PREC_COEF and FastMath.lnMant (LN_MANT).
  jcompat.rs   org.apache.commons.math3.random.MersenneTwister (seeding and
               next(int)) and BitsStreamGenerator.nextInt(int).

These files were changed with respect to the originals: they were translated
from Java to Rust by the peabiru authors, only the parts listed above were
kept, and the lookup tables are stored as literal IEEE-754 bit patterns.

