7. Sample data
==============================================================================

The R and Python packages include a small network of the area around Avenida
Paulista, in Sao Paulo, cut from the sample data of r5r 2.5.0
(inst/extdata/spo in the r5r package):

  spo_osm.pbf     Cut from r5r's spo_osm.pbf, an extract of OpenStreetMap.
                  Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under
                  the Open Database License (ODbL),
                  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  spo_gtfs.zip    r5r's spo.zip without shapes.txt: a frequency-based GTFS
                  feed whose agency.txt names the agency SPTRANS,
                  http://www.sptrans.com.br.
  spo_points.csv  27 points of r5r's spo_hexgrid.csv, the hexagonal grid of
                  Sao Paulo, with their population and opportunity counts.

r5r distributes these files as part of its package, under "GPL (>= 3) | MIT
+ file LICENSE" (the MIT notice is in section 4), and states no other
licence or source for them; peabiru gives the same attribution.

