8. Population grid
==============================================================================

gtfs/gpwv3-quarter-buffer-boolean.bits.deflate holds, compressed, the grid
gtfs-lib uses to flag GTFS stops in places with almost no population
(SuspectStopLocationError): R5's resource
com/conveyal/gtfs/storage/gpwv3-quarter-buffer-boolean.asc, quarter-degree
cells marked where the population density of the cell or of a neighbouring
cell exceeds 5 people per square kilometre. As R5's source states, Conveyal
derived it from the 2015 UN-adjusted population density of the Gridded
Population of the World, version 3 (GPWv3), at 1/4 degree resolution:

    Center for International Earth Science Information Network - CIESIN -
    Columbia University. Gridded Population of the World, Version 3
    (GPWv3). Palisades, NY: NASA Socioeconomic Data and Applications
    Center (SEDAC). http://sedac.ciesin.columbia.edu/data/collection/gpw-v3

which is distributed under a Creative Commons Attribution licence. peabiru
keeps the grid's cells unchanged, only stored as bits.
